author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Core collection reads and mutations accept --format json and toon before or after the command; Existing command-local formats and contributed command vocabularies remain intact; Invalid encoding and read-shaping mutation controls refuse without writes; SDK contracts and sandboxed regressions prove the compatibility grammar
goal: project management = context management
objective: Remove cross-command encoding traps without duplicating renderer logic
value: Agents can reuse one learned encoding spelling across reading context and recording work
why_now: GH-1480 records repeated failed reads and first mutation attempts on the current release
parent: pm-srns
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "SDK-owned conditional --format json|toon aliases now cover core item collections and lifecycle writes, prefix/suffix/inline invocation, runtime discovery, domain-format preservation, and empty internal contracts."
expected_result: "Item reads and writes reuse the format spelling without rejected round trips or persistence on invalid requests, while existing command-specific formats and package command vocabulary remain valid."
actual_result: "10662 tests passed; exact full-source 100/100/100/100 coverage; both linked tests passed; static, startup/transport, graph/history, mutation, package-first and packed npx/bunx gates passed. Latest pm-changelog 2026.10.17 installed and checked. Closure is carried in the reviewed branch."
